text: "---\nmodule: \"03-SALES-CLOSING\"\npart: \"E\"\ntitle: \"Closing Rituals\"\nversion: \"2026.05\"\nstatus: \"Production-Ready\"\n---\n\n# 03E: Closing Rituals\n\n> **Core Principle:** The close is not the end. It is the beginning of the relationship. How you handle the transition from \"yes\" to \"work started\" sets the tone for everything that follows.\n>\n> *\"Get upfront project payment. For payments use: Payoneer, Wise.\"* — Him Singh\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [The \"YES\" Confirmation](#1-the-yes-confirmation)\n2. [Payment Collection](#2-payment-collection)\n3. [Kickoff Ritual](#3-kickoff-ritual)\n4. [Invoice Templates](#4-invoice-templates)\n5. [Payment Protection](#5-payment-protection)\n6. [AI Prompts](#6-ai-prompts)\n7. [Action Checklist](#7-action-checklist)\n\n---\n\n## 1. The \"YES\" Confirmation\n\n### The Email Confirmation\n\n```\nSubject: [Project Name] — Let's Get Started!\n\nHi [Name],\n\nFantastic! I'm excited to work with [Company] on [project].\n\nHere's what happens next:\n\n1. **SOW Attached:** Please review and reply \"YES\" to confirm\n2. **Deposit Invoice:** I'll send within 24 hours of your confirmation\n3. **Kickoff Call:** We'll schedule for [day after deposit received]\n4. **Project Portal:** I'll set up [Notion/Slack/Trello] for updates\n\n**Project Summary:**\n- Scope: [Brief description]\n- Timeline: [Weeks] (kickoff [date] → delivery [date])\n- Investment: $[Amount] (50% deposit + 25% milestone + 25% final)\n- My direct email: [your email]\n- Emergency contact: [your phone]\n\n**What I need from you before kickoff:**\n- [ ] Data access credentials\n- [ ] Brand guidelines (if applicable)\n- [ ] Stakeholder contact list\n- [ ] Any existing documentation\n\nQuestions? Just reply to this email.\n\nLet's build something great.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\n```\n\n### The Mutual Agreement \"YES\" [Him Singh Style]\n\nFor smaller projects or fast-moving clients:\n\n```\nSubject: [Client] x [Your Name] | Mutual Agreement for [Project]\n\nHi [Name],\n\nSo this is a mutual agreement for partnership between [Client] and \nus on delivering [specific work].\n\nUnder this agreement we mutually agree on:\n\nWe provide:\n1) [Deliverable 1] — [specification]\n2) [Deliverable 2] — [specification]\n3) [Deliverable 3] — [specification]\n4) [X] revision rounds free of cost\n5) Additional revisions at $[Amount] each\n6) Payments: [upfront/milestone]\n7) Delivered by [date]\n\nYou provide:\n1) [Client responsibility 1]\n2) [Client responsibility 2]\n\nKindly reply \"YES\" to confirm and agree.\n\nIf you have any questions, feel free to ask.\n\nCheers,\n[Your name]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Payment Collection\n\n### Payment Methods (2026)\n\n| Method | Fees | Speed | Best For | Setup |\n|--------|------|-------|----------|-------|\n| **Payoneer** | 1% (free $50 bonus on signup) | 2-5 days | International | Easy |\n| **Wise** | 0.5-1% | 1-2 days | US/EU/UK | Easy |\n| **Contra** | $29/contract | Instant | Platform clients | Built-in |\n| **Stripe** | 2.9% + $0.30 | 2 days | Direct clients | Developer setup |\n| **Bank Transfer** | $15-50 wire fee | 3-7 days | Enterprise | Account details |\n| **PayPal** | 3-4% | Instant | Small projects | Easy |\n\n### The Payment Request Email\n\n```\nSubject: Invoice #[Number] — [Project Name] — Deposit\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThank you for confirming the project! Here's your deposit invoice.\n\n**Invoice Details:**\n- Invoice #: [Number]\n- Date: [Date]\n- Due Date: [Date]\n- Amount Due: $[Amount]\n- Description: [Project Name] — Deposit (50%)\n\n**Payment Options:**\n→ Payoneer: [link]\n→ Wise: [link]\n→ Bank Transfer: [details attached]\n\n**What happens after payment:**\n1. I'll send kickoff meeting invite within 24 hours\n2. Project portal access will be shared\n3. Work begins on [start date]\n\n**Questions?** Reply to this email or text [your phone].\n\nLooking forward to delivering great results.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\n```\n\n### Payment Follow-Up Schedule\n\n| Day | Action | Tone |\n|-----|--------|------|\n| **Due date** | Send friendly reminder | Helpful |\n| **+3 days** | Second reminder + phone call | Concerned |\n| **+7 days** | Pause work, notify of delay | Professional |\n| **+14 days** | Final notice, mention contract terms | Firm |\n| **+30 days** | Collections or legal (last resort) | Formal |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Kickoff Ritual\n\n### The Kickoff Call Agenda (30 minutes)\n\n| Time | Topic | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| **0-5 min** | Introductions + rapport | Build comfort |\n| **5-10 min** | Review SOW + success criteria | Align on expectations |\n| **10-15 min** | Access + logistics | Remove blockers |\n| **15-20 min** | Communication norms | Set boundaries |\n| **20-25 min** | Q&A | Address concerns |\n| **25-30 min** | Next steps + calendar | Lock in timeline |\n\n### Communication Norms Setup\n\n```\n\"To make sure this runs smoothly, here are my communication norms:\n\n• **Updates:** Every [Tuesday/Friday] via [email/Slack]\n• **Response time:** Within 24 hours on business days\n• **Urgent issues:** Text/call [number] — I'll respond within 2 hours\n• **Feedback:** Please provide within 48 hours of delivery\n• **Scope changes:** Email only — no Slack scope creep\n\nDoes this work for your team?\"\n```\n\n### The Project Portal Setup\n\n**Tools:** Notion, Trello, Linear, Asana, ClickUp\n\n**Portal Contents:**\n- [ ] Project overview + SOW\n- [ ] Timeline with milestones\n- [ ] Deliverables tracker\n- [ ] Meeting notes archive\n- [ ] Resource folder (brand assets, data access)\n- [ ] FAQ / Decision log\n\n---\n\n## 4. Invoice Templates\n\n### Professional Invoice Template\n\n```\nINVOICE\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nFrom: [Your Name / Business Name]\n[Address]\n[Email] | [Phone]\n[Tax ID if applicable]\n\nTo: [Client Name / Company]\n[Address]\n[Contact Name]\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nInvoice #: [Number]\nInvoice Date: [Date]\nPayment Due: [Date]\nProject: [Project Name]\nSOW Reference: [SOW Version]\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n| Item | Description | Qty | Rate | Amount |\n|------|-------------|-----|------|--------|\n| 1 | [Service 1] | [X] | $[Rate] | $[Amount] |\n| 2 | [Service 2] | [X] | $[Rate] | $[Amount] |\n| 3 | [Service 3] | [X] | $[Rate] | $[Amount] |\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSubtotal: $[Amount]\nTax [X%]: $[Amount]\nDiscount: -$[Amount]\n\nTOTAL DUE: $[Amount] [Currency]\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nPayment Methods:\n□ Payoneer: [link]\n□ Wise: [link]\n□ Bank Transfer: [details]\n\nTerms: Net 7. Late payments subject to 1.5% monthly fee.\n\nNotes: [Any special instructions]\n\nThank you for your business!\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n```\n\n### Invoice Tools (2026)\n\n| Tool | Cost | Best For | Features |\n|------|------|----------|----------|\n| **HelloBonsai** | $19/mo | Freelancers | Proposals + contracts + invoicing |\n| **Wave** | Free | Simple invoicing | Basic, US/Canada only |\n| **FreshBooks** | $17/mo | Small business | Time tracking + expenses |\n| **QuickBooks** | $30/mo | Growing business | Full accounting |\n| **Invoice Simple** | Free | Mobile-first | Quick, simple |\n| **Google Sheets** | Free | Manual tracking | Custom templates |\n| **Canva** | Free | Design-heavy | Beautiful invoices |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Payment Protection\n\n### The Deposit Rule\n\n| Project Size | Deposit % | When Due |\n|--------------|-----------|----------|\n| Under $2,000 | 100% upfront | Before work begins |\n| $2,000-$10,000 | 50% upfront | Before work begins |\n| $10,000-$25,000 | 50% upfront + 25% milestone | Milestone defined in SOW |\n| Over $25,000 | 33/33/33 | Start, midpoint, delivery |\n\n### The Milestone Rule\n\nNever deliver final work before final payment:\n\n```\n\"The final deliverables will be transferred upon receipt of \nfinal payment. You'll receive:\n• Full source code\n• Documentation\n• Deployment credentials\n• Training materials\n\nOnce payment is confirmed, I'll send everything within \n2 hours.\"\n```\n\n### Escalation for Non-Payment\n\n| Stage | Action | Timeline |\n|-------|--------|----------|\n| **1. Friendly** | Email reminder + phone call | Day 3 past due |\n| **2. Formal** | Written notice referencing SOW | Day 7 past due |\n| **3. Pause** | Stop all work, notify of delay | Day 10 past due |\n| **4. Final** | Demand letter, mention legal | Day 21 past due |\n| **5. Legal** | Small claims or collections | Day 30+ past due |\n\n**Prevention > Cure:**\n- Always get deposit before starting\n- Use milestone payments for large projects\n- Include late fees in SOW\n- Keep communication documented\n- Know when to walk away (sunk cost fallacy)\n\n---\n\n## 6. AI Prompts\n\n### Prompt 1: Closing Email Writer\n\n```\nAct as a client onboarding specialist.\n\nProject details:\n- Client: [COMPANY]\n- Project: [NAME]\n- Price: $[AMOUNT]\n- Timeline: [WEEKS]\n- Payment: [STRUCTURE]\n\nWrite a closing email that:\n1. Celebrates the \"yes\" (enthusiastic but professional)\n2. Lists 4-5 clear next steps\n3. Includes what client needs to provide\n4. Sets communication expectations\n5. Attaches SOW (reference it)\n6. Ends with forward momentum\n\nTone: Excited, organized, professional.\n```\n\n### Prompt 2: Invoice Generator\n\n```\nAct as a billing specialist for freelancers.\n\nInvoice details:\n- Invoice #: [NUMBER]\n- Client: [COMPANY]\n- Project: [NAME]\n- Amount: $[AMOUNT]\n- Description: [WHAT THIS PAYMENT IS FOR]\n- Payment methods: [PAYONEER/WISE/BANK]\n\nGenerate:\n1. Professional invoice (formatted)\n2. Payment request email\n3. Payment reminder (day 3 past due)\n4. Final notice (day 14 past due)\n\nMake it clean, professional, and legally sound.\n```\n\n### Prompt 3: Kickoff Agenda Creator\n\n```\nAct as a project manager.\n\nProject type: [AI/ML / Web Dev / Data / etc]\nClient: [COMPANY TYPE]\nTeam size: [NUMBER]\nDuration: [WEEKS]\n\nCreate a kickoff meeting agenda:\n1. 30-minute structured agenda (minute-by-minute)\n2. 5 questions to ask the client\n3. 3 things to communicate about your process\n4. 2 potential concerns to surface early\n5. Follow-up email template\n\nMake it specific to [project type], not generic.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Action Checklist\n\n### Day 1: Confirmation\n\n- [ ] Send \"YES\" confirmation email\n- [ ] Attach SOW (if not already sent)\n- [ ] Send deposit invoice within 24 hours\n- [ ] Set up project portal (Notion/Trello/Slack)\n- [ ] Calendar kickoff call (after deposit)\n\n### Day 2-3: Preparation\n\n- [ ] Confirm deposit received\n- [ ] Send kickoff meeting invite\n- [ ] Prepare kickoff agenda\n- [ ] Set up project tracking system\n- [ ] Create folder structure for deliverables\n\n### Day 4-7: Kickoff\n\n- [ ] Conduct kickoff call (use agenda)\n- [ ] Document meeting notes\n- [ ] Confirm client provided all access/logistics\n- [ ] Send summary email with next steps\n- [ ] Begin work (if all blockers cleared)\n\n### Ongoing: Financial Hygiene\n\n- [ ] Send invoices on schedule (milestone dates)\n- [ ] Track payment status in spreadsheet\n- [ ] Follow up on late payments (3-day rule)\n- [ ] Reconcile payments monthly\n- [ ] Save all invoices for tax purposes\n\n---\n\n> **Next Module:** [04-PROJECT-DELIVERY →](../../freelancer-project-delivery/SKILL.md)\n>\n> *\"The close is where trust becomes contract. Handle it with care.\"*\n\n---\n\n*Module 03E | Closing Rituals | Version 2026.05*\n"
